  <h1>How I work</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    I run coding agents on my own home server under written rules. Risky changes pass an independent verifier and a
    clean-context reviewer; routine changes skip them. Private data never leaves the tailnet.
  </p>

  <h2>The pipeline</h2>
  <ol class="loop">
    <li><strong>Task.</strong> Notion Uptime Tasks board; I set priority, the supervisor picks the next task.</li>
    <li><strong>Rules.</strong> Conventions, permissions (agent alone / asks / human only) and runbooks live in a git wiki; changes via PR.</li>
    <li><strong>Executor.</strong> <code>/make</code>: intent → procedure → plan → change. Model picked per risk tier.</li>
    <li><strong>Checks.</strong> Risk-tiered: small changes → verify script + CI → auto-merge; system changes → verifier GO/STOP before, PASS/FAIL after, clean-context review before merge.</li>
    <li><strong>Memory.</strong> Every session logged (metadata only). A weekly job distills decisions/errors into <code>## Rules</code>; agent-memory RAG answers "why".</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Five rules</h2>
  <ul class="checks">
    <li>A check that cannot run is a failure.</li>
    <li>Two human gates: spec and merge (merge is automatic when CI + checks pass; I review ~every 5th PR or anything critical).</li>
    <li>Agents commit to branches; merge, admin, secrets — human only.</li>
    <li>Hooks log metadata, never prompts or file contents.</li>
    <li>Nothing is reachable from the internet; all access via Tailscale.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What runs today</h2>
  <ul class="checks">
    <li><strong>Machine:</strong> M920q, WSL2, one tmux session per project (Claude Code). Laptop is a thin client. Phone via SSH + tmux.</li>
    <li><strong>Control:</strong> Stream Deck+ → own deck-server (session per key).</li>
    <li><strong>Guard:</strong> git-guard — global git hooks, secret and leak scan on every commit, all repos.</li>
    <li><strong>Local models:</strong> jev API (OpenAI-compatible router) + Ollama on CPU for sensitive requests.</li>
    <li><strong>Records:</strong> Notion (what &amp; why), GitHub PRs (how), one JSON line per routed request with a canary test.</li>
    <li><strong>Backup:</strong> nightly restic to a local disk, restore-tested.</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="muted source">
    The repositories named here are private. The case studies describe the projects that run on this platform.
  </p>
</Base>

